WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.480
When I was a kid.

2
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.640
every adult I knew shared
one thing in common;

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.840
a gap in their lives
when everything appeared uncertain

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.800
and time itself seemed
to stand still.

5
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.840
When they talked about it.
they simply called it The War.

6
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.480
For six dark years.
the world was on fire.

7
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.280
cities were demolished.
and whole populations threatened.

8
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.560
When would the war end?
No-one knew.

9
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.080
How would it end?

10
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.640
No-one knew.

11
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.640
Life was in stasis.

12
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.880
The War is now a part
of our culture.

13
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.120
portrayed in movies
and on television.

14
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.080
in novels and history books.

15
00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.520
The Allies usually defeat
the enemy and save the world.

16
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:56.640
But the grim reality of the war
is almost impossible to comprehend.

17
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.640
Over 65 million people are killed.
the majority civilians.

18
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.800
Everyone fought some version
of The War.

19
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.520
beginning with
the mothers and fathers.

20
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.440
who sent their children overseas.
not knowing when. or if.

21
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.400
they would ever see them again.

22
00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.160
And. of course. the soldiers.
sailors. airmen. and marines.

23
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.160
often just a bunch of kids.

24
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.480
who served with honour and bravery
to liberate enslaved peoples

25
00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.400
and preserve human dignity.

26
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.680
In doing so.

27
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.440
they saved that which is most
precious and valued by us all.

28
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.800
Freedom.

29
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.640
The Second World War is
the largest event in human history.

30
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.240
No part of the globe is unaffected.

31
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.360
World War Two changed everything.
for all of us.

32
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.120
All wars change the world.

33
00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.880
But none of them change the world
like the Second World War did.

34
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.280
Japan's on the march;
Germany's on the march.

35
00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:01.000
No-one can imagine the nightmare
they're about to unleash.

36
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.000
the most destructive war
in human history.

37
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.080
Suddenly the world
is turned upside down.

38
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.400
And all hell is let loose.

39
00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.840
The West is stunned
by the speed of the advance.

40
00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.160
You get the Allies
led by the big three.

41
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.760
Roosevelt. Churchill. Stalin.

42
00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.800
Men who are dealing with
immensely complicated questions.

43
00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.880
It's the biggest military
operation of human history.

44
00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.920
The Allies have to come together.

45
00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.760
not just militarily
but industrial scale.

46
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.480
it's a global perspective.

47
00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.480
They have to fight
in every climate from the Arctic

48
00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.880
to the jungles of the Pacific

49
00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.400
to the deserts of Africa
and the depths of the ocean.

50
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.320
But there was no certainty
of victory;

51
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.200
it was going to be
a horrific bloodbath.

52
00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.800
We see humans
at their absolute worst.

53
00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.000
how they treat other human beings.

54
00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.280
And we see them
at their absolute best.

55
00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.240
willing to give their lives
that others might live.

56
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.080
World War Two was a struggle
in which there could be one victor

57
00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.320
and one vanquished.

58
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.074
