59
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.320
{\an8}<i>Sometimes the most monumental
events begin without fanfare.</i>

60
00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.120
<i>Before the world wakes.</i>

61
00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.160
<i>And so it is.
on the 1st of September 1939</i>

62
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.440
<i>as dawn breaks over
a sleeping city on the Baltic Sea.</i>

63
00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.680
<i>that the bloodiest conflict
in all history begins.</i>

64
00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.720
<i>This is the National Programme
from London.</i>

65
00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.880
{\an8}<i>Germany has invaded Poland.</i>

66
00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.520
<i>Heavy outbreaks of fighting
along the German Polish frontier.</i>

67
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.520
<i>In just a matter of hours.
a million and a half men...</i>

68
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.520
<i>...1.300 planes...</i>

69
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.640
<i>...and 2.750 tanks...</i>

70
00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.640
<i>...cross the Polish border
at lightning speed.</i>

71
00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.200
September 1st 1939.

72
00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.880
{\an8}A storm breaks over Poland.

73
00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.840
The Germans are racing through
with tanks and with artillery

74
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.520
following up with the infantry
and accompanied by the Luftwaffe.

75
00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.760
{\an8}And all of a sudden people were
waking up to the sound of tanks

76
00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.040
{\an8}rumbling through the town. not
really knowing what was happening.

77
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.480
You're going to see waves
of trucks and mechanised

78
00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.000
and motorised vehicles.

79
00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.080
It looks a bit like
a science fiction novel.

80
00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.480
like all those novels written
in the '20s and '30s

81
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.760
about what the war of the future
would look like.

82
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.880
And suddenly in 1939.
the future is now.

83
00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:24.040
<i>At 11am. Hitler arrives
at a Berlin opera house.</i>

84
00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.680
<i>where he's gathered the Reichstag.</i>

85
00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.560
This is the moment Hitler
has been waiting for all his life.

86
00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.920
He's been the leader
of the Nazi Party since 1921.

87
00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.480
He came to power in '33.
He rearms the country in '35.

88
00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.040
And since then.
it's been prepare. prepare. prepare.

89
00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.680
But Hitler wants a war.

90
00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.920
<i>The invasion follows months
of diplomatic tension</i>

91
00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.560
<i>over a strip of land known
as the Polish Corridor.</i>

92
00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.640
<i>Land that had once been part
of Germany...</i>

93
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.040
<i>...but was ceded to Poland
to give her access to the sea</i>

94
00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.880
<i>after the first World War.</i>

95
00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.200
<i>Twenty years earlier.</i>

96
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:41.280
<i>global leaders gathered
in the French city of Versailles</i>

97
00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.400
<i>to sign the historic treaty
ending that war.</i>

98
00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.440
<i>After four years of brutal fighting.</i>

99
00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.200
<i>an alliance led
by Britain and France.</i>

100
00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.200
<i>and supported by the United States.
emerged victorious.</i>

101
00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:00.160
<i>Germany. its military exhausted
and its people near starvation.</i>

102
00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:01.560
<i>had lost.</i>

103
00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:05.200
<i>And now.
they would pay the price of defeat.</i>

104
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.400
The Treaty of Versailles takes
territories away from Germany.

105
00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.280
It strips Germany of populations
and raw materials.

106
00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.640
It turns the entire German merchant
marine over to the allies.

107
00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.000
It imposes reparations
on the Germans.

108
00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:24.000
The Allies were attempting to
limit the future power of Germany.

109
00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:26.880
The effects of the First World War
were so grave.

110
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.280
{\an8}They were so catastrophic
that no-one wanted to see

111
00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.760
{\an8}a repeat of that.

112
00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.280
<i>One young Austrian corporal
fighting for the German army</i>

113
00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.760
<i>is Adolf Hitler.</i>

114
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.560
<i>Like many. he is shocked
by the way the war ends.</i>

115
00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.920
Your average German was surprised
by the news of the armistice

116
00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.400
because it happened so suddenly.

117
00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.800
{\an8}The army was still in the field.
and there was the sense

118
00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.360
{\an8}that we haven't been invaded
and thoroughly beaten.

119
00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.680
It was personally
a tragedy for Hitler.

120
00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.680
He heard the news of the armistice

121
00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.480
when he was still ill
from injuries sustained in battle.

122
00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.080
{\an8}He did not process
the end of the war well.

123
00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.320
{\an8}He did not accept
the defeat of Germany.

124
00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.760
<i>Surviving soldiers come home
angry and confused.</i>

125
00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:15.960
Frankly. the response of many
of them is disillusionment.

126
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.960
Four years at the front. I managed
to dodge all those bullets.

127
00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.640
and now I came home
and this is what I fought for.

128
00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.840
When Hitler comes back
from the war.

129
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.600
he learns to talk to former soldiers
who are now disgruntled

130
00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:33.040
and begins to feel the fact that
he's actually quite a good speaker.

131
00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.680
He attends a meeting
of a small group.

132
00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:42.600
which will become the
National Socialist German Workers.

133
00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.840
or Nazi Party.

134
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.240
He finds something attractive.
this is a party of grievance.

135
00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.760
talking about how
Germany could be transformed.

136
00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.840
and Germany could be made
powerful again.

137
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.080
In 1921.
Hitler's talent for public speaking

138
00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.520
makes him the leader
of this tiny party.

139
00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.520
<i>Hitler's first move is
an attempted coup</i>

140
00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.080
<i>against the Bavarian state
government in Munich...</i>

141
00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.920
<i>...but it fails
and he's arrested for treason.</i>

142
00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.520
<i>At his trial.</i>

143
00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.640
<i>the Judge allows Hitler to publicly
share his movement's grievances.</i>

144
00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.520
<i>against war guilt. reparation.
and communism.</i>

145
00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:24.520
<i>In jail.
he publishes his memoir Mein Kampf.</i>

146
00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.600
<i>or My Struggle.</i>

147
00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.480
<i>With Hitler's notoriety.
Nazi Party membership grows</i>

148
00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:37.000
<i>as Germany's Weimar Republic
moves through the unstable '20s.</i>

149
00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.800
<i>The economy is burdened
by heavy war reparations.</i>

150
00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:46.240
<i>In 1923.
the cost of one loaf of bread</i>

151
00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.680
<i>rockets from
three Marks to 80 billion.</i>

152
00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:55.840
<i>The years that follow
are unstable. chaotic.</i>

153
00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.240
<i>Hitler's Nazi Party fuels
racial hatred against Jews</i>

154
00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.240
<i>and fears about communism.</i>

155
00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:07.360
<i>Then.
just as the economy is recovering.</i>

156
00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.000
<i>the Great Depression throws
six million Germans out of work.</i>

157
00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:15.840
People in Germany are confused.
bewildered. unhappy.

158
00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.480
And so there's a real opening
for a leader who will speak

159
00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:20.440
all these lines perfectly
and talk about

160
00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:22.440
how I'm going to bring
the Germans back together.

161
00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.040
<i>In the 1932 elections.
Germany is deeply divided.</i>

162
00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:34.040
<i>But President von Hindenberg.
backed by conservative businessmen.</i>

163
00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.720
<i>appoints Hitler Chancellor
to run the government</i>

164
00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.920
<i>at the beginning of 1933.</i>

165
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.440
In 1934.

166
00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:47.360
Hitler declares that he will now
continue to be Chancellor

167
00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:50.560
and take over the role
of the President as well.

168
00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.720
He's transformed what was
a democracy in Germany

169
00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.640
into a one-party
and a one-man dictatorship.

170
00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.680
He's become the German leader.
the Fuhrer.

171
00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:07.920
<i>His first promise as Fuhrer
is to reclaim the land</i>

172
00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.080
<i>Germany lost at Versailles.</i>

173
00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:14.360
<i>He seizes The Rhineland.
Austria. and the Sudetenland.</i>

174
00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:17.040
<i>German-speaking parts
of Czechoslovakia.</i>

175
00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:22.680
<i>By 1938. just four years later.
he's reshaped the map of Europe.</i>

176
00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.400
<i>Desperate to avoid another war.</i>

177
00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.960
<i>Britain and France allow Hitler
to expand his empire.</i>

178
00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.320
In 1938. at Munich.
Neville Chamberlain.

179
00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.600
the British Prime Minister.

180
00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:39.040
and the French actually
made a deal with Hitler.

181
00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:41.880
{\an8}What he wanted was
the Sudetenland of Czechoslovakia.

182
00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.640
{\an8}The British had said. fine.

183
00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.640
we'll just dismantle
an entire country to keep you happy.

184
00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.520
<i>But when Hitler
turns to Poland.</i>

185
00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.080
<i>the West finally takes a stand.</i>

186
00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:57.120
<i>The Poles have already endured
centuries of foreign rule.</i>

187
00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:02.440
<i>The country regains its independence
as part of the Versailles treaty.</i>

188
00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:06.560
<i>but its new borders now include
20.000 square miles</i>

189
00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.000
<i>of what had been German land.</i>

190
00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.960
<i>In summer 1939.</i>

191
00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.640
<i>the British and the French sign
a guarantee with the Poles.</i>

192
00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:21.880
<i>promising military assistance
if the Germans invade.</i>

193
00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.120
Hitler. speaking to his officers.
they're asking him questions.

194
00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.080
What was the attitude of the West
going to be if you attack Poland?

195
00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.360
And he snorted.
'Don't worry.' he said.

196
00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:36.360
'I've seen my opponents at Munich.
They're little worms.'

197
00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:40.640
<i>Hitler doesn't believe the West
has the will to go to war...</i>

198
00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.280
<i>...so he moves across the border.</i>

199
00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.440
<i>ready to invade with the full force
of the Nazi Wehrmacht.</i>

200
00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.080
<i>In the first 24 hours
of the invasion...</i>

201
00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:12.640
<i>...the Germans take out railroads.
bridges. and airfields.</i>

202
00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.720
<i>The destruction paves the way</i>

203
00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.400
<i>for their army to advance
deep into Poland.</i>

204
00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:25.720
{\an8}The Poles have a modern army.

205
00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.720
It's the fifth-largest army
in the world.

206
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.280
And it's equipped with modern tanks.

207
00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:36.200
with all sorts of artillery.
and armoured trains.

208
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.400
But Hitler has been putting
almost all his resources

209
00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.800
into equipping the military.

210
00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:47.880
The Poles were outgunned by
the Germans who had 3-to-1 tanks.

211
00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:49.280
and 5-to-1 aeroplanes

212
00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:52.640
so there's no question that
the Germans were a superior force.

213
00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.560
<i>Despite those odds.</i>

214
00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:59.000
<i>the Poles are determined
to defend their country.</i>

215
00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.640
{\an8}<i>- Everyone had to help;</i>

216
00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:07.440
{\an8}<i>and soldiers conscripted civilians
on the street. putting them to work.</i>

217
00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:10.680
{\an8}<i>I saw one man who was stopped
six times on his way home</i>

218
00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.600
<i>with a loaf of bread.</i>

219
00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.840
<i>The Poles remain resilient.</i>

220
00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.520
<i>But the question is
what will Britain and France do?</i>

221
00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:29.160
<i>Here as ever in critical days
we're seeing the coming</i>

222
00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.000
<i>and going of the leaders
of the country.</i>

223
00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.880
The British and French had
an alliance with the Poles.

224
00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:36.800
They have to defend Poland.

225
00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:39.720
But they're not
militarily prepared to do so.

226
00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.080
and they're not
mentally prepared to do so.

227
00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:46.520
{\an8}The home fronts in Britain and
France are dead set against war.

228
00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.840
<i>British Prime Minister
Neville Chamberlain tells Parliament</i>

229
00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.640
<i>he's considering issuing
an ultimatum.</i>

230
00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:57.720
<i>But many feel he's backtracking
on his promise to Poland.</i>

231
00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:03.080
This is a profound injury
to British honour.

232
00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:06.120
that if we don't
act and declare war.

233
00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:09.840
no other country will ever trust
a treaty with Britain ever again.

234
00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.960
<i>Britain delivers an ultimatum
to Berlin</i>

235
00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:16.240
<i>on the morning of
September 3rd 1939.</i>

236
00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.520
<i>Hitler has until 11am
to withdraw his forces.</i>

237
00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.200
<i>It's ignored.</i>

238
00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:32.240
{\an8}<i>- This morning.
the British Ambassador in Berlin</i>

239
00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:36.040
{\an8}<i>handed the German government
a final note.</i>

240
00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:41.960
<i>and consequently. this country
is at war with Germany.</i>

241
00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.160
<i>In cities across Britain.</i>

242
00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:51.200
<i>air-raid sirens signal
a strange new era.</i>

243
00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:55.560
<i>and millions of gas masks
are sent to British homes.</i>

244
00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:00.760
<i>Across the Atlantic.</i>

245
00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:04.080
<i>America is just emerging
from the Great Depression</i>

246
00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.280
<i>and not prepared for war.</i>

247
00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.560
<i>The peacetime army is small.</i>

248
00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:16.400
<i>And neutrality laws make it
nearly impossible to aid the Allies.</i>

249
00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.720
<i>In the White House.</i>

250
00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.680
<i>the press gathers for one of
President Roosevelt's</i>

251
00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.400
<i>Fireside Chats.</i>

252
00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:28.320
I have said not once
but many times

253
00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.320
{\an8}that I have seen war.

254
00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.920
{\an8}and that I hate war.

255
00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:36.840
I say that again and again.

256
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:40.320
I hope the United States
will keep out of this.

257
00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:44.960
And I give you assurance
and reassurance.

258
00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:49.880
that every effort of your government
will be directed toward that end.

259
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.520
Most Americans.

260
00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.640
when they're asked should
the United States get involved.

261
00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.080
{\an8}90% of Americans
say absolutely not.

262
00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.360
But Franklin Delano Roosevelt
is watching...

263
00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.040
what's happening in Europe
very closely.

264
00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:09.800
The question is about freedom
and democracy.

265
00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.040
He understands what is at stake.

266
00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:18.040
<i>In Germany. Hitler is surprised
when Britain and France declare war.</i>

267
00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.080
When the British
declaration of war is made.

268
00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:24.840
Hitler receives it in silence
and for a couple of moments.

269
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.640
he stares at his foreign minister.
Ribbentrop.

270
00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:30.800
and then. with a quite vicious tone
to his voice.

271
00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.840
he says. 'What now?'

272
00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:42.440
<i>Despite the British
and French declaration.</i>

273
00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:45.600
<i>Hitler continues his master plan
for Poland</i>

274
00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.600
<i>and sends in the Luftwaffe.</i>

275
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:54.160
<i>Hitler's air force is led
by a trusted member</i>

276
00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.160
<i>of his inner circle.</i>

277
00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.960
<i>Field Marshal Hermann Goering.</i>

278
00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.080
Goering is a German celebrity.

279
00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.680
In WWI. he was the head of
the Flying Circus.

280
00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:08.800
Der Fliegende Zirkus.
This elite group of fighter pilots.

281
00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:12.280
And so he's well known in Germany.

282
00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.800
He's very handsome.
very charismatic guy.

283
00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.040
But there's also a very dark side
to Goering.

284
00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:21.040
He feels deeply embittered
by the way the war ended.

285
00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.240
And he falls under Hitler's spell.

286
00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:27.640
And he's able to get huge
appropriations from Hitler

287
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:29.680
for Luftwaffe procurement.

288
00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:33.480
<i>Goering's elite pilots
are young</i>

289
00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:36.160
<i>and have spent thousands of hours
in training.</i>

290
00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:40.480
<i>From the cockpits of heavy bombers.
they drop explosives.</i>

291
00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:46.520
<i>But it's the precision dive bombers
that wreak the most terror.</i>

292
00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.240
The Sturzkampfflugzeug.

293
00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:53.240
the Stuka as it's usually
abbreviated.

294
00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.600
you know. it's not
a particularly swift craft.

295
00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:59.600
But they dive at
an almost 90-degree angle...

296
00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:04.000
...and literally drop
a bomb in your lap.

297
00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:10.600
And there's even a bit
of psy war here as well.

298
00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:14.280
As they're coming down on you.
there's a siren screaming.

299
00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:21.160
In Poland. there are pilots flying
at low altitude

300
00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.120
{\an8}who can see women
and children fleeing the roads.

301
00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:27.720
who actually target them
deliberately.

302
00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:38.680
Polish civilians experience
modern war

303
00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.000
in an unbelievably horrifying way.

304
00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.400
They see people killed.
They see bodies all around them.

305
00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.040
It's a nightmare.

306
00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:56.440
<i>Poland is being destroyed.</i>

307
00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:04.400
<i>It is not clear when. or even if.</i>

308
00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:07.640
<i>Britain and France can send
forces to help.</i>

309
00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.200
<i>On day three.</i>

310
00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:26.920
<i>Adolf Hitler boards his heavily
armoured private train.</i>

311
00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:28.400
<i>the Amerika.</i>

312
00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:32.920
<i>He named it after his admiration
for the way America settled</i>

313
00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:34.600
<i>a vast continent.</i>

314
00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.880
<i>Now. travelling towards Poland.</i>

315
00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:41.000
<i>he looks out on the territory
he means to conquer.</i>

316
00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.440
<i>Land stretching deep
into Eastern Europe.</i>

317
00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:50.120
<i>Lebensraum. Living space.
for his new German Empire.</i>

318
00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:53.600
<i>This is his and Germany's destiny.</i>

319
00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:57.560
{\an8}Hitler talks about
a thousand-year Reich.

320
00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:00.360
Its borders would stretch
from the Atlantic in the west

321
00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:03.760
to Scandinavia in the north.
and the Mediterranean in the south.

322
00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.800
Poland and the lands to the east
play a special role

323
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.440
in Hitler's foreign policy plans.

324
00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.400
They're wide-open spaces.

325
00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:13.000
farmland as far
as the eye could see.

326
00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:17.320
<i>In order to achieve
this vast empire.</i>

327
00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:20.040
<i>Germans must clear out
the people living there.</i>

328
00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:22.520
<i>in a remorseless race war.</i>

329
00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:26.960
Adolf Hitler's whole worldview

330
00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:30.360
is based on a kind
of neo-Darwinism.

331
00:22:30.520 --> 00:22:35.120
{\an8}in which every single act
is a biological struggle.

332
00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:38.320
Warfare between different races.

333
00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.880
He believes that the Aryan race.
the Germans.

334
00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:46.200
is the superior race on the planet.

335
00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:49.840
it's destined to rule Europe
and indeed the world.

336
00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:53.280
<i>Until now. Hitler's main target</i>

337
00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:56.080
<i>has been
Germany's Jewish population.</i>

338
00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:00.440
<i>Under his orders.
they lost their status as citizens.</i>

339
00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.440
<i>had their wealth
and property seized.</i>

340
00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:05.520
<i>and many were forced into exile.</i>

341
00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:10.320
Hitler believes that humanity is
locked in this existential battle

342
00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:13.560
{\an8}between Aryans.
as he describes them. and Jews.

343
00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:17.360
And Jews are supposedly responsible
for all of society's

344
00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:19.240
and the world's ills.

345
00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.960
So who is responsible for
the German loss in World War One?

346
00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.400
{\an8}Jewish people.

347
00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:28.960
{\an8}Who is responsible
for economic inequality?

348
00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:30.200
Jewish people.

349
00:23:30.360 --> 00:23:34.600
They control media. newspapers.
all the businesses.

350
00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:37.440
The reason you are poor is because
they are hoarding money.

351
00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.320
What the Nazis are seeking to do
at this stage

352
00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.600
is to make life so unpleasant.
so difficult for Jewish people

353
00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:45.840
within the Reich
that they want to leave.

354
00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:51.000
<i>Hitler also wants to remove
the Slavs of Eastern Europe.</i>

355
00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:53.400
<i>including the people of Poland.</i>

356
00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:03.720
<i>Day four. Hitler reaches
the Polish frontlines.</i>

357
00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.600
<i>where he holds a photo opportunity
with his troops.</i>

358
00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:10.840
He makes himself very visible.
goes to the front

359
00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.560
and he's greeted by these thousands
and thousands of people.

360
00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:17.760
They're all vying with one another
to get close to Adolf Hitler.

361
00:24:18.480 --> 00:24:21.960
He's fought in World War One.
He's a battle-tested leader.

362
00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:25.160
{\an8}He's taking back
historic German territory.

363
00:24:25.320 --> 00:24:26.840
{\an8}He's built the armed forces.

364
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.880
They listen to him.

365
00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:35.480
These German soldiers marching on
Poland believe in Germany's destiny.

366
00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:40.120
That they will be the creators
of the great new Germany.

367
00:24:41.360 --> 00:24:43.520
{\an8}This is the first action
they've had militarily

368
00:24:43.680 --> 00:24:46.520
{\an8}since the black day
of the German army in 1918.

369
00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:50.800
And it is an average infantryman
from the First World War

370
00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:52.240
who's leading it.

371
00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:55.600
So this is redemption.

372
00:24:55.760 --> 00:24:59.760
20 years after what never should
have happened. happened.

373
00:25:02.720 --> 00:25:07.280
<i>Shadowing his invading forces
is another wing of the Nazi regime.</i>

374
00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:10.120
<i>The protection squadron.</i>

375
00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:14.440
<i>In German. the Schutzstaffel. Or SS.</i>

376
00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:19.280
<i>They were Hitler's personal
bodyguards as he rose to power...</i>

377
00:25:20.840 --> 00:25:23.160
<i>...but under the leadership
of Heinrich Himmler.</i>

378
00:25:23.320 --> 00:25:27.080
<i>they become a paramilitary outfit
at the heart of the regime.</i>

379
00:25:29.040 --> 00:25:33.600
Himmler is somebody
who has a sadistic streak.

380
00:25:33.760 --> 00:25:35.560
He's quite meek.
He's not particularly assuming.

381
00:25:35.720 --> 00:25:37.440
He's certainly not very
physically impressive.

382
00:25:37.600 --> 00:25:40.840
But he's somebody who's got
a burning desire to achieve things.

383
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.640
He gets drawn into the Nazi loop.

384
00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:45.520
And then over a period of time.

385
00:25:45.680 --> 00:25:47.600
he eventually takes control
of the SS.

386
00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:52.160
Himmler has developed the SS from
a small kind of a bodyguard unit

387
00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:54.200
that's supposed to really
protect Hitler

388
00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:58.640
into a vast. militarised force.

389
00:26:00.040 --> 00:26:05.200
<i>In Poland. the SS units fan out
across the newly occupied territory.</i>

390
00:26:05.360 --> 00:26:08.480
<i>as does a special wing of the SS.</i>

391
00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:10.400
<i>the Einsatzgruppen.</i>

392
00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:13.720
<i>Mobile death squads.</i>

393
00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:24.080
<i>In September 1939.
during the Invasion of Poland.</i>

394
00:26:24.240 --> 00:26:29.120
<i>the Nazi Einsatzgruppen are under
orders to neutralise any opposition.</i>

395
00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:34.120
The Einsatzgruppen
are specifically set up

396
00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:39.080
{\an8}to go into towns. villages
and other areas of Poland.

397
00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:40.840
to kill civilians.

398
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:43.000
That's their only job.

399
00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:47.280
Professors. landowners. politicians.
newspaper editors.

400
00:26:47.440 --> 00:26:49.680
these sorts of people.
they were targeted and killed

401
00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:51.800
because these were the people
who were identified

402
00:26:51.960 --> 00:26:54.120
as possibly leading
some sort of resistance

403
00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:55.680
against the German forces.

404
00:26:55.840 --> 00:26:58.960
And this is something that the Poles
could not have known yet

405
00:26:59.120 --> 00:27:01.160
on those first days of the invasion.

406
00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:03.720
that this wasn't just going to be
a military invasion.

407
00:27:03.880 --> 00:27:07.400
but this was also going to be
a war of annihilation.

408
00:27:10.520 --> 00:27:14.080
For Hitler. this is a chance
not just to destroy Poland.

409
00:27:14.240 --> 00:27:18.000
{\an8}but to clear Poland.
to crush the Polish people

410
00:27:18.160 --> 00:27:19.400
{\an8}who are Slavs.

411
00:27:19.560 --> 00:27:23.440
and Slavs in the Nazi ideology
are Untermenschen. under humans.

412
00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:26.440
But it's more than that.
There are also Jews in Poland.

413
00:27:27.760 --> 00:27:31.960
<i>For centuries. Poland has been
home to millions of Europe's Jews.</i>

414
00:27:32.120 --> 00:27:34.800
<i>who fled there to avoid
religious persecution.</i>

415
00:27:35.640 --> 00:27:39.440
The Jews originally settled there
because it was the freest kingdom

416
00:27:39.600 --> 00:27:40.720
in Europe.

417
00:27:40.880 --> 00:27:45.240
Now they found themselves
in a terrifying. murderous trap.

418
00:27:46.520 --> 00:27:49.960
The SS drag Orthodox Jewish men
out into the streets

419
00:27:50.120 --> 00:27:52.640
and they desecrate their clothes
and their hair.

420
00:27:53.320 --> 00:27:55.080
They smash up synagogues.

421
00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:59.000
They are seeking to amplify
the terror that they've sought

422
00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:02.360
{\an8}to develop within the Reich
towards Jews within Poland.

423
00:28:03.880 --> 00:28:08.040
<i>These acts of brutality
escalate into public executions.</i>

424
00:28:10.480 --> 00:28:13.360
<i>In the town of Konskie
on September 12th.</i>

425
00:28:13.520 --> 00:28:16.560
<i>German troops order local Jews
to the town square...</i>

426
00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:20.200
<i>...to dig the grave
of a German soldier.</i>

427
00:28:23.800 --> 00:28:28.360
This rather humiliating
forced gravedigging exercise

428
00:28:28.520 --> 00:28:31.000
quickly descends into a pogrom.

429
00:28:32.400 --> 00:28:35.360
{\an8}Jews are shot. You know. they try
and run away from the scene.

430
00:28:35.520 --> 00:28:37.520
they're quickly apprehended.

431
00:28:39.040 --> 00:28:42.800
And in total.
22 Jews are killed on that day.

432
00:28:43.680 --> 00:28:46.240
This was happening across Poland.

433
00:28:48.120 --> 00:28:51.320
The brutal mass murder
of innocent civilians.

434
00:28:57.840 --> 00:28:59.840
<i>Nine days into the invasion.</i>

435
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.520
<i>Britain and France continue
to mobilise their forces.</i>

436
00:29:03.680 --> 00:29:06.160
<i>Civilians are being killed
in the streets.</i>

437
00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:08.080
<i>but the army isn't defeated.</i>

438
00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:11.240
<i>With their capital city. Warsaw.
now the target.</i>

439
00:29:12.160 --> 00:29:14.680
<i>Two Polish armies stage
a counterattack</i>

440
00:29:14.840 --> 00:29:16.160
<i>to the west of the city.</i>

441
00:29:16.320 --> 00:29:20.480
<i>Polish cavalry and reconnaissance
tanks drive German forces back</i>

442
00:29:20.640 --> 00:29:24.120
<i>12-and-a-half miles.
in the Battle of the Bzura River.</i>

443
00:29:24.840 --> 00:29:27.480
{\an8}You know. all too often
the Polish campaign is talked about

444
00:29:27.640 --> 00:29:30.560
{\an8}as some kind of pushover.
But the Poles fought hard.

445
00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:32.560
The classic stereotype
of the Poles

446
00:29:32.720 --> 00:29:34.920
is that they're all in their horses
with sabres drawn.

447
00:29:35.080 --> 00:29:37.800
riding toward tanks
who are just shooting them down.

448
00:29:37.960 --> 00:29:40.760
This is absurd.
The Poles were very sophisticated.

449
00:29:40.920 --> 00:29:45.520
Very finely trained soldiers.
extremely brave.

450
00:29:47.240 --> 00:29:50.440
<i>As Poles fight
under German bombardment...</i>

451
00:29:51.760 --> 00:29:55.720
<i>...Prime Minister Neville Chamberlain
and French Premier Edward Daladier</i>

452
00:29:55.880 --> 00:30:00.920
<i>meet for a Supreme War Council.
and reach a grave decision.</i>

453
00:30:01.960 --> 00:30:05.840
Daladier and Chamberlain agree
to leave Poland to its fate.

454
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:09.880
{\an8}They also adopt formally what
they call the long war strategy.

455
00:30:10.040 --> 00:30:12.840
{\an8}the idea that they have superior
resources to Germany.

456
00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:14.240
and that over time.

457
00:30:14.400 --> 00:30:17.160
those resources will come to bear
in the Allies' favour.

458
00:30:17.960 --> 00:30:20.840
Although the statement
that is given to the world's press

459
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.280
is one of wholehearted support.

460
00:30:23.440 --> 00:30:27.360
Poland is essentially cast
to the four winds.

461
00:30:28.400 --> 00:30:31.440
<i>There is one British politician
who has always wanted</i>

462
00:30:31.600 --> 00:30:34.400
<i>to take a more aggressive position
against the Nazis.</i>

463
00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:38.960
<i>Appointed to the new War Cabinet
is Hitler's most vocal critic</i>

464
00:30:39.120 --> 00:30:40.280
<i>in the West.</i>

465
00:30:40.440 --> 00:30:43.920
<i>First Lord of the Admiralty.
Winston Churchill.</i>

466
00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:47.120
Throughout the 1930s.

467
00:30:47.280 --> 00:30:50.920
Churchill had spoken up with concern
about German rearmament.

468
00:30:51.080 --> 00:30:54.320
about the failure to take effective
measures to enforce

469
00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:56.240
the Versailles Treaty.

470
00:30:56.400 --> 00:31:01.160
{\an8}It's clear now that Germany couldn't
be trusted as a diplomatic partner.

471
00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:11.000
<i>Two weeks into the invasion.</i>

472
00:31:13.600 --> 00:31:17.640
<i>The Poles seem abandoned. and their
counteroffensive is collapsing.</i>

473
00:31:19.800 --> 00:31:24.200
<i>The German third. eighth and tenth
armies encircle Warsaw.</i>

474
00:31:29.800 --> 00:31:34.120
<i>The capital is a city of palaces.
churches. and opera houses.</i>

475
00:31:34.280 --> 00:31:36.760
<i>the heart of the Polish nation.</i>

476
00:31:38.160 --> 00:31:43.200
<i>But now.
Warsaw is in ruins and under siege.</i>

477
00:31:48.880 --> 00:31:52.040
Bombs were falling and everybody
was trying to help get people out

478
00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:53.240
of the rubble.

479
00:31:53.400 --> 00:31:56.040
When your roof is burning.
when your children are in hospital

480
00:31:56.200 --> 00:31:58.680
because they've been bombed.
I mean these are shocking moments.

481
00:31:59.760 --> 00:32:02.760
<i>American photographer
and cameraman Julien Bryan</i>

482
00:32:02.920 --> 00:32:07.040
<i>is in Poland's capital.
filming suffering and defiance.</i>

483
00:32:08.280 --> 00:32:10.320
<i>He pleads for Poland.</i>

484
00:32:11.360 --> 00:32:14.480
{\an8}<i>- President Roosevelt
and the people of America.</i>

485
00:32:14.640 --> 00:32:16.440
{\an8}<i>listen to my story.</i>

486
00:32:17.480 --> 00:32:20.280
<i>America must act. It must help.</i>

487
00:32:21.480 --> 00:32:25.800
<i>As help is called for. there is
an army preparing to sweep in.</i>

488
00:32:27.280 --> 00:32:29.120
<i>They're not coming from the West.</i>

489
00:32:30.640 --> 00:32:31.920
<i>But from the East.</i>

490
00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:48.360
On the 17th of September.

491
00:32:48.520 --> 00:32:52.560
Joseph Stalin calls the German
Ambassador to the Kremlin

492
00:32:52.720 --> 00:32:55.600
{\an8}and says. we're going
to invade eastern Poland.

493
00:33:01.080 --> 00:33:04.360
<i>Poland's fate isn't sealed
just by the Nazis.</i>

494
00:33:04.520 --> 00:33:08.320
<i>The communists of Soviet Russia
also sense opportunity;</i>

495
00:33:08.480 --> 00:33:11.680
<i>and so does
their all-powerful master.</i>

496
00:33:13.120 --> 00:33:17.320
Stalin is one of the most
extraordinary figures in the history

497
00:33:17.480 --> 00:33:19.120
of the 20th century.

498
00:33:19.280 --> 00:33:22.720
From the very beginning of
the Russian Revolution in 1917.

499
00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:26.240
he's been part of the tiny clique
that's been running Russia

500
00:33:26.400 --> 00:33:31.360
and has emerged as the dominant
leader of the whole Soviet Union.

501
00:33:31.520 --> 00:33:35.880
The inner circle called him Hoziam:
the Master. the Boss.

502
00:33:36.040 --> 00:33:38.960
But in public. he was the Vozhd:
the leader.

503
00:33:39.640 --> 00:33:43.760
But he was a tough man.
a morbid man. a mysterious man.

504
00:33:43.920 --> 00:33:48.120
He learnt the hard way
in the Russian Civil War

505
00:33:48.280 --> 00:33:51.960
{\an8}that you operate ruthlessly.
you sacrifice. you attack.

506
00:33:52.120 --> 00:33:54.360
{\an8}you show no quarter to your enemies.

507
00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:58.400
Stalin saw the world
in geopolitical terms.

508
00:33:58.560 --> 00:34:02.760
He recognised that the Soviet Union
couldn't survive. isolated.

509
00:34:02.920 --> 00:34:04.640
surrounded by adversaries.

510
00:34:04.800 --> 00:34:08.880
He had to play the poker game
of diplomacy and war.

511
00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:11.680
And the players were
the Western democracies

512
00:34:11.840 --> 00:34:14.600
led by England and France.
and the dictatorships.

513
00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:18.720
His great fear was that
the two sides would gang up

514
00:34:18.880 --> 00:34:21.520
against him
and destroy the Soviet Union.

515
00:34:21.680 --> 00:34:24.560
And all of his decisions
came from this fear.

516
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:27.840
<i>In August 1939.</i>

517
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:31.320
<i>just one week
before Germany invades Poland.</i>

518
00:34:31.480 --> 00:34:33.880
<i>Joseph Stalin shocked the world</i>

519
00:34:34.040 --> 00:34:37.600
<i>when he signed a non-aggression pact
with Adolf Hitler.</i>

520
00:34:38.520 --> 00:34:41.040
The revelation of
the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact

521
00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:44.000
causes mayhem
in the Western capitals.

522
00:34:44.160 --> 00:34:47.160
It changes everything.
It's a complete shock.

523
00:34:48.320 --> 00:34:51.600
For the last sort of five years.
the two dictatorships.

524
00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:54.320
Nazi Germany and Stalinist Russia.

525
00:34:54.480 --> 00:34:58.200
had been pouring excrement
over each other in the media.

526
00:34:58.360 --> 00:35:01.400
They had been calling each other
every name under the sun.

527
00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:06.120
And for each. the other was
the quintessential enemy

528
00:35:06.280 --> 00:35:07.720
of everything they believed.

529
00:35:07.880 --> 00:35:10.840
And now suddenly. there's thawing.

530
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:15.480
and the next thing you know.
Ribbentrop is flying to Moscow.

531
00:35:17.200 --> 00:35:20.920
In August 1939.
by signing a pact with Hitler.

532
00:35:21.080 --> 00:35:24.760
Stalin helps to ensure that
the Second World War will break out.

533
00:35:24.920 --> 00:35:27.160
{\an8}In fact.
it makes it virtually a certainty

534
00:35:27.320 --> 00:35:28.840
{\an8}that such a war will break out.

535
00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:33.080
<i>The pact promises a decade
of non-aggression</i>

536
00:35:33.240 --> 00:35:34.880
<i>between the two regimes.</i>

537
00:35:35.800 --> 00:35:39.160
<i>But there's another. secret.
protocol which carves up</i>

538
00:35:39.320 --> 00:35:42.520
<i>Eastern Europe.
sharing the land between them.</i>

539
00:35:43.440 --> 00:35:45.120
<i>First up is Poland.</i>

540
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:50.840
{\an8}Neither the Germans nor
the Soviets wanted Poland to exist.

541
00:35:51.840 --> 00:35:53.880
They both saw it as an affront.

542
00:35:54.040 --> 00:35:57.160
Poland had historically been
a province of the Russian Empire.

543
00:35:57.320 --> 00:35:59.240
The Soviets want that back

544
00:35:59.400 --> 00:36:02.480
as a buffer against the stronger
Germany that's emerging.

545
00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:06.320
The division of Polish territory
favoured the Soviets.

546
00:36:06.480 --> 00:36:08.760
who got more territory
than the Germans did.

547
00:36:10.160 --> 00:36:13.400
So it's actually the Soviet invasion
of eastern Poland

548
00:36:13.560 --> 00:36:16.280
that decides the fate of Poland.

549
00:36:24.480 --> 00:36:27.760
<i>The Red Army pours into
Poland's eastern provinces.</i>

550
00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:34.320
<i>They too carry orders to eradicate
Polish leaders and culture.</i>

551
00:36:35.480 --> 00:36:38.240
When the Red Army goes
into eastern Poland.

552
00:36:38.400 --> 00:36:41.120
they are accompanied.
inevitably by the secret police.

553
00:36:41.280 --> 00:36:45.000
the NKVD.
and they arrest all these people.

554
00:36:45.160 --> 00:36:48.880
Writers. diplomats.
aristocrats. army officers.

555
00:36:49.880 --> 00:36:53.080
Some of them are killed instantly.
some of them are deported.

556
00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:56.680
and a large number of them.
between 20.000 and 30.000.

557
00:36:56.840 --> 00:37:01.000
are stowed in camps
near the Katyn woods.

558
00:37:01.760 --> 00:37:05.320
All of these people are to be
secretly executed.

559
00:37:05.480 --> 00:37:07.040
shot in the back of the head.

560
00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:17.040
<i>On September 22nd 1939.
in the town of Brest-Litovsk.</i>

561
00:37:17.200 --> 00:37:22.600
<i>Nazi and Soviet generals gather
to watch a parade of both armies.</i>

562
00:37:26.240 --> 00:37:29.160
There's this free mingling
of German and Soviet forces.

563
00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:31.880
the two sides are sort of mixing.
sharing cigarettes.

564
00:37:32.040 --> 00:37:33.320
sharing anecdotes.

565
00:37:33.480 --> 00:37:36.040
And they even develop
almost a slang between them

566
00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:39.200
{\an8}'Germanski Bolsheviki.
together strong'.

567
00:37:40.720 --> 00:37:44.560
If you're a Polish person.
to see these two people

568
00:37:44.720 --> 00:37:48.880
that have always been dangerous
on both sides of you.

569
00:37:49.040 --> 00:37:54.040
{\an8}working together to see that Poland
once again disappears.

570
00:37:54.200 --> 00:37:56.480
you had to feel
like there's no help close by.

571
00:37:57.680 --> 00:38:02.240
<i>As Poland burns.
and her enemies celebrate.</i>

572
00:38:02.400 --> 00:38:04.400
<i>one city resists.</i>

573
00:38:06.400 --> 00:38:07.720
<i>Warsaw.</i>

574
00:38:13.280 --> 00:38:17.160
<i>Despite weeks of assault.
Warsaw has not yet surrendered.</i>

575
00:38:17.320 --> 00:38:21.040
<i>Surviving Polish troops
rush to the capital</i>

576
00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:25.480
<i>where 300.000 soldiers
and civilians hold the city.</i>

577
00:38:26.760 --> 00:38:28.320
<i>To break the resistance.</i>

578
00:38:28.480 --> 00:38:32.000
<i>Goering orders the largest air raid
ever seen.</i>

579
00:38:45.720 --> 00:38:49.640
Goering levels Warsaw with
no regard for civilian casualties.

580
00:38:49.800 --> 00:38:53.320
{\an8}They strew thousands of pounds of
high-explosive and incendiary bombs.

581
00:38:53.480 --> 00:38:57.520
{\an8}firebombs over Warsaw.
and they reduce it to rubble.

582
00:39:07.040 --> 00:39:09.400
It is the largest
incendiary bombing

583
00:39:09.560 --> 00:39:11.360
that the world has ever seen.

584
00:39:12.280 --> 00:39:14.560
Air raids last
for the entirety of the day.

585
00:39:14.720 --> 00:39:16.160
{\an8}People are trapped
in their basements.

586
00:39:16.320 --> 00:39:18.640
{\an8}They're trapped in courtyards.
They're trapped in stairwells.

587
00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:21.920
Those who crawl out
when the bombardment is over.

588
00:39:22.080 --> 00:39:24.680
there's no water.
There's nothing to feed them.

589
00:39:28.560 --> 00:39:31.600
{\an8}20% of the city is destroyed
in one way or another.

590
00:39:31.760 --> 00:39:35.600
And about 18.000 people are injured
or killed in these bombardments.

591
00:39:36.440 --> 00:39:39.400
And the city finally
has to surrender.

592
00:40:05.680 --> 00:40:08.640
<i>In London.
Winston Churchill warns his country</i>

593
00:40:08.800 --> 00:40:10.560
<i>that this is just the beginning.</i>

594
00:40:11.760 --> 00:40:15.760
{\an8}<i>- Poland has been overrun by two
of the great Powers</i>

595
00:40:15.920 --> 00:40:17.720
{\an8}<i>which held her in bondage</i>

596
00:40:17.880 --> 00:40:19.680
<i>for 150 years.</i>

597
00:40:19.840 --> 00:40:24.440
<i>but were unable to quench
the spirit of the Polish nation.</i>

598
00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:28.520
<i>The heroic defence of Warsaw</i>

599
00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:33.120
<i>shows that the soul of Poland
is indestructible.</i>

600
00:40:35.960 --> 00:40:39.480
<i>The British Empire
and the French Republic</i>

601
00:40:39.640 --> 00:40:43.520
<i>have been at war with Nazi Germany
for a month tonight.</i>

602
00:40:46.200 --> 00:40:48.960
<i>Directions have been given
by the Government</i>

603
00:40:49.120 --> 00:40:52.640
<i>to prepare for a war
of at least three years.</i>

604
00:40:57.040 --> 00:40:59.960
<i>But Churchill has received
a signal of hope.</i>

605
00:41:00.840 --> 00:41:04.480
<i>A few weeks earlier.
President Roosevelt sent him a note.</i>

606
00:41:04.640 --> 00:41:07.800
<i>congratulating him on his new role
in the War Cabinet.</i>

607
00:41:07.960 --> 00:41:10.920
<i>and opening up a secret line
of communication.</i>

608
00:41:12.200 --> 00:41:16.200
{\an8}Once Germany invades Poland.
Roosevelt infers that this war

609
00:41:16.360 --> 00:41:19.320
{\an8}is going to be sizeable
in its scope

610
00:41:19.480 --> 00:41:21.760
{\an8}and that the United States
is probably going to need

611
00:41:21.920 --> 00:41:23.480
to intervene at some point.

612
00:41:24.120 --> 00:41:27.880
Churchill has this reputation
of being a fighter.

613
00:41:28.560 --> 00:41:31.760
It's really telling that Roosevelt
seeks him out

614
00:41:31.920 --> 00:41:34.800
rather than Chamberlain
at this critical juncture

615
00:41:34.960 --> 00:41:36.560
at the beginning of
the Second World War.

616
00:41:37.440 --> 00:41:40.640
So there's this relationship
that develops between

617
00:41:40.800 --> 00:41:43.960
Franklin Delano Roosevelt
and Winston Churchill.

618
00:41:44.120 --> 00:41:46.280
There's an understanding
on the part of Roosevelt

619
00:41:46.440 --> 00:41:50.200
that there is someone
in the leadership of Great Britain

620
00:41:50.360 --> 00:41:52.160
who understands what's at stake.

621
00:41:52.320 --> 00:41:55.960
{\an8}and just how dangerous
this moment is.

622
00:41:57.440 --> 00:42:01.480
It's not simply about
the German invasion of Poland.

623
00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:06.840
They are two men
who are united in their belief

624
00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:11.320
that Adolf Hitler is perhaps
the most dangerous man on the planet

625
00:42:12.960 --> 00:42:14.280
{\an8}After the surrender.

626
00:42:14.440 --> 00:42:17.760
{\an8}Hitler travels to Warsaw
to survey the ruins.

627
00:42:19.480 --> 00:42:21.480
{\an8}He points at the utter destruction

628
00:42:21.640 --> 00:42:23.800
{\an8}and tells the officers
who are with him...

629
00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.880
{\an8}...this is the real meaning of war.

630
00:42:31.280 --> 00:42:32.840
In less than a month.

631
00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:36.080
a major European nation
has been removed from the map.

632
00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:40.680
It will be engulfed in darkness
for most of the next six years.

633
00:42:40.840 --> 00:42:44.360
And it's only the beginning
as Hitler looks to the west.

